---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { STANDARD_MOQ_PCS, PUBLIC_COMPANY_NAME, PUBLIC_EMAIL } from '../data/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="Quotation & Order Terms | HAN XING" description="Model approval, minimum quantities, samples, payment and delivery terms to agree in writing before ordering HAN XING motor capacitors.">
  <article class="procurement-page procurement-privacy">
    <section class="procurement-hero"><div class="container procurement-privacy-wrap"><p class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Order terms</p><h1>Quotation and order terms</h1></div></section>
    <div class="container procurement-privacy-wrap procurement-privacy-body">
      <p>Last updated: <time datetime="2026-10-14">14 October 2026</time>. This page explains the items to agree before an order. Business contact: {PUBLIC_COMPANY_NAME}, <a href={`mailto:${PUBLIC_EMAIL}`}>{PUBLIC_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
      <section><h2>Product selection and approval</h2><p>Series ranges cover several configurations. Before ordering, agree the exact model, current datasheet, dimensioned drawing and approval sample for the required rating, size and terminals.</p><a class="card-link" href="/products/">Compare product series</a></section>
      <section><h2>Quotation and minimum quantity</h2><p>The standard MOQ is {STANDARD_MOQ_PCS.toLocaleString('en-US')} pieces. Ask for the minimum, sample charges, freight and sample preparation time that apply to the quoted configuration. The written offer must state prices, currency, payment schedule, delivery terms, production lead time and quotation validity.</p><a class="card-link" href="/oem/">Sample and OEM approval</a></section>
      <section><h2>Seller, quality and delivery</h2><p>The quotation and contract should identify the legal seller and manufacturer. Agree the tests, acceptance limits, certificates, approved marking and packing required for the order. Record destination and delivery responsibilities in writing, keeping shipping estimates separate from actual carrier-handover records.</p><a class="card-link" href="/about/#supplier-records">Supplier identity information</a><a class="card-link" href="/factory/packing-and-dispatch/">Packing and dispatch</a></section>
      <section><h2>Warranty and existing orders</h2><p>Agree warranty duration, exclusions, inspection arrangements and remedies in writing before accepting the order. For an existing order, send the order reference, model, batch markings and a description of the issue.</p><a class="card-link" href="/contact/?request=after-sales#inquiry-form">Ask about an existing order</a></section>
      <section><h2>Changes, cancellations and returns</h2><p>Agree how specification changes, cancellations, returns and non-conforming goods will be handled before placing an order, including any approval steps, time limits and costs. For an existing order, refer to its agreed terms and contact the seller before returning goods.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Governing terms and disputes</h2><p>Specify the governing law, dispute-resolution process and document precedence in the order agreement.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Inquiries and order agreement</h2><p>The contact form creates a draft to send from your email or WhatsApp app. It does not place an order, take payment or send the message. Order terms are established by the signed contract and agreed written quotation; this page lists the items to agree.</p><a class="button" href="/contact/">Prepare an inquiry</a><a class="card-link" href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy notice</a></section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
